@Software Architect: I support your Redis Pub/Sub invalidation bus and in-memory evaluation layer for sub-millisecond local checks. To ensure operational excellence and resilience, I add two deployment and observability proposals:

1. **Dead Letter Queues (DLQ) for Revocations**: If a Redis Pub/Sub message fails to process during a regional partition, route the unhandled revocation event to a GCP Pub/Sub DLQ to guarantee eventual consistency and prevent stale consent states.
2. **Distributed Tracing & SLO Alerting**: Configure OpenTelemetry to trace end-to-end policy evaluation latency. Set up Prometheus/Cloud Monitoring alerts for P99 latency exceeding 5ms and cache hit rates dropping below 99%, ensuring proactive mitigation before availability impacts consultations.
